{"type": "thinking", "text": "Both photos have empty Captured. So perhaps the seed has no EXIF capture date and the code should fall back... Hmm.\n\nWait. Maybe the \"capture date\" is displayed in the details panel only when EXIF has a date. Since these seeds have no EXIF date, no row appears. That isn't necessarily a bug.\n\nBut the task explicitly lists \"Photo details panel: the capture date is now read from the photo's EXIF metadata\" as a change in this build, strongly implying there's a display of capture date in the details panel. Maybe it's missing = bug (the regression). Hmm, but perhaps the display is the top bar date, and maybe it's showing the \"Added\" date as fallback while EXIF has a different value? We don't know seed EXIF.\n\nLet me think about the data: Photos named big.jpg (1,500,000 bytes) and huge.jpg (2,500,000 bytes). Added/Modified Nov 14, 2026 11:19. The viewer top bar shows \"November 14 · 11:19 AM\" — same. If EXIF capture date existed, it might be something like \"November 14, 2023\". The fact that top bar matches the file date suggests no EXIF or fallback.\n\nHmm, maybe I'm overthinking. Perhaps the \"photo details panel\" is the \"Details\" sheet and the capture date is expected in the \"Image Properties\" section. There's Resolution but no \"Captured\". The change note might describe a feature: \"capture date is now read from photo's EXIF metadata\" — this could be about the top bar date in photo viewer. And the test would be: if EXIF date exists, show it. Since seeds may have EXIF date set to something distinct... but we see empty Captured in editor, which suggests the app doesn't read EXIF at all! That could be the bug: the editor (and details) show no capture date even though the file has EXIF DateTimeOriginal. But we can't read files... We could use \"Set Current Time\" to set it and see.\n\nActually here's a thought: maybe the seed photos DO have EXIF with a capture date, but the app displays the file's \"Added\" date instead in the top bar, and the editor shows empty because of a bug in reading EXIF. To distinguish, we could set the capture date via the editor to a distinct value, save, and see if the details/top bar picks it up. That tests reading of EXIF written by the app. If it then displays correctly, the read path works; the initial empty could just be no EXIF.\n\nHmm. But the change says \"read from the photo's EXIF metadata\" — maybe the bug is that it reads the wrong tag or falls back incorrectly. Hard to detect.\n\nLet me broaden testing first. Let me test metadata editing (title/description), then capture date setting, then check details view. Use big.jpg.\n\nLet me type a title. Tap Title field and type \"TestTitleQA\". Then save. See if editor? Then reopen to verify persisted.\n\nActually, careful: editing metadata via \"Android will ask before changing media owned by another app\" — there may be a permission dialog. Let's see.\n\nLet me start with Description tab: set Title. I'll go to Description tab."}
