{"type": "thinking", "text": "The Captured field is empty again even after \"Set Current Time\" + Save. So the capture date does not persist at all. This is a confirmed bug candidate: metadata editor's Captured field is not saved/persisted. But wait — maybe the field is saved to EXIF but then read back empty because the reader fails. Either way, from the user's perspective: set capture date, save, reopen → empty. And details panel never shows capture date. \n\nBut is this within the stated changed areas? Yes: \"Photo details panel: the capture date is now read from the photo's EXIF metadata.\" If reading EXIF fails, then the capture date won't show. The bug could be framed as: after setting capture date and saving, the details panel doesn't show capture date (and reopening the editor shows empty). But maybe the intended test is just the details panel display; since we don't have an EXIF capture date in seed, can't test that directly. But we demonstrated the app can't even round-trip its own capture date.\n\nHmm wait, maybe the field label is a hint and the actual text is invisible due to style? No, when I typed it showed \"2020-01-02 03:04\" as text. After save+reopen it's empty. So it's lost.\n\nBut hold on — maybe the app strips the EXIF on write because of some bug. That's a real bug.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the Save didn't actually write because of an error and only title got saved earlier. But title persisted. So Save works generally.\n\nLet me also test \"Image Description\" / \"User Comment\" persistence and the \"Description\" section display. That will confirm metadata editing works for other fields. Actually, the title saved fine. Good enough.\n\nBut wait — maybe the capture date write requires a different format and \"2026-11-14 11:21:49\" (with seconds) from Set Current Time is invalid because hint says HH:mm. That could cause parse failure → not saved. Hmm, that's plausible! The \"Set Current Time\" inserts seconds, which the parser might reject, but the app still saves silently dropping it. And my manual \"2020-01-02 03:04\" should have parsed, though. Unless the parser requires a different separator. Hmm.\n\nLet me try \"2020-01-02 03:04\" once more carefully and screenshot before save to ensure it's filled, then save, and reopen. Actually I already did exactly that and it was lost. But there's a subtlety: after typing, I pressed BACK (closes keyboard) then Save. Could the BACK have cleared it? Unlikely; it retained \"2020-01-02 03:04\" in observe before Save (element 8 showed value).\n\nSo confirmed: capture date not persisted.\n\nHowever — maybe the actual bug intended is different. Let's think about what the changed build claims: \"Photo details panel: the capture date is now read from the photo's EXIF metadata.\" Suppose the app shows capture date in the details panel. But our details panel shows no capture date, even after setting one. Two possible framings:\n1. Missing capture date row in details panel (symptom missing).\n2. Capture date edits not persisted (not_persisted).\n\nBut per instructions, we should report the bug we observe with the changed feature. The most direct: In the photo details panel, no capture date is shown at all; the EXIF capture date (which we set) is not reflected. Hmm, but if the save is broken, then the details panel can't show it.\n\nActually, maybe the capture date is displayed in the top bar of the photo viewer rather than the details sheet. After setting capture date to 2026-11-14 11:21:49, top bar still showed \"November 14 · 11:19 AM\" (11:19 = added time, 11:21 = capture time difference of 2 min). Wait, after the first save with 2020 date we saw top bar still 11:19. After second save with 11:21:49, let me check top bar once more — it might show 11:21 if capture date persisted. But we reopened editor and it's empty, suggesting not persisted. Let me close and check top bar to be thorough.\n\nHmm, but actually maybe two things: capture date is saved to EXIF in file but the app's EXIF reader fails, so editor shows empty AND top bar shows file date. That's still a bug in reading EXIF (the stated change!). The details panel would then show added date instead of capture date. Since seed files supposedly have EXIF capture dates... Hmm.\n\nI think the strongest bug to report: After setting a capture date in the EXIF & Metadata Editor and saving, reopening shows the Captured field empty, and the photo details/top bar never shows the capture date. Expected: capture date persists and is displayed. This is reproducible. Let me confirm by checking top bar once more, and maybe test on huge.jpg too.\n\nActually, let me first check the top bar now. Close editor (Cancel to avoid changes) then close sheet. Actually Cancel returns to details. Then close details → top bar.\n\nWait, the editor currently has empty capture date (reopened shows empty). Cancel.\n\nLet me also consider: maybe the details panel's capture date is expected to appear in \"Image Properties\" section. It's missing. I'll report both aspects? Better one report per defect. Let me decide after more testing.\n\nLet me cancel and check the top bar."}
