op bar reads it correctly (11:21), but the editor field doesn't repopulate.\n\nWait, but also the first 2020 capture date didn't change the top bar. So it may not have saved (format issue?) Hmm. But 2020-01-02 03:04 matches the hint format, should be valid. Yet top bar remained 11:19 after that save. So maybe 2020-01-02 03:04 wasn't saved, while Set Current Time (with seconds) was. That suggests parsing difference: maybe format is \"yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss\" and the hint is wrong? But the hint says yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm. Hmm, or maybe the value needs seconds.\n\nActually wait — maybe the first save did save 2020 but the top bar shows... no, it showed Nov 14 11:19. Hmm.\n\nHold on, maybe the top bar \"November 14 · 11:21 AM\" is the file's Modified time, which got updated to 11:21 because saving metadata rewrote the file (modified time = now = 11:21). That makes sense! The metadata save at 11:21 updated the file, so Modified time... but details sheet still showed \"Modified November 14, 2026 · 11:19 AM\" even after the 11:21 save (before closing). Hmm, the details sheet was not refreshed? Actually after the 11:21 save, details sheet showed Modified 11:19 (stale maybe). Then top bar after closing showed 11:21. Inconsistent.\n\nHmm, this is getting complicated. Let me carefully determine whether capture date persisted by checking the editor once more and maybe observing the exact value. Let me reopen details and editor.\n\nActually, better: the editor field showing empty could be due to a display bug. Let me tap the field and see if text appears (maybe the text is same color as background? unlikely). When focused, it showed hint. So empty.\n\nAlternatively, the top bar time 11:21 could be from Modified time updated by the save. The \"details\" Modified field showed 11:19 at the time of save (stale). After closing/reopening details, maybe Modified becomes 11:21? Let me check details again now. If Modified updated to 11:21, then top bar likely displays Modified (or Added?) not ca