rnatively, use the \"Copy to album\" flow? It also may create album. Hmm.\n\nSimplest: create albums and accept that they may have items. To have multiple non-empty albums, we'd need photos. We have 2 photos. Could use \"Copy to album\" to duplicate photos into new albums, creating multiple non-empty albums. That changes data (duplicates) but can be deleted.\n\nHmm, maybe empty albums persist. Let me test: create Alpha (moves big.jpg to Alpha), then create Mike (moves big.jpg to Mike). Check Albums: is Alpha still there empty? Let's see.\n\nActually, the album list in move dialog might include empty albums too (since \"Zeta\" remains after moving out? we'll see). Let me just create Alpha and Mike and observe.\n\nLet me start from Albums → open big.jpg (Zeta card, element 4). In album Zeta, tap big.jpg, then More → Move → New album → \"Alpha\" → Create. Repeat for Mike.\n\nActually, creating from the move dialog is efficient. Let me do:\n1. Tap Zeta card → big.jpg → More → Move to album → New album → type Alpha → Create. (big.jpg now in Alpha)\n2. Then from Media open big.jpg → More → Move → New album → Mike → Create. (big.jpg in Mike)\n3. Then open big.jpg → More → Move → observe album list order.\n\nLet's go."}
