{"type": "thinking", "text": "Captured empty again. So the typed capture date is NOT persisted at all. The \"Set Current Time\" value also not shown in editor. But maybe \"Set Current Time\" wrote MediaStore DATE_TAKEN (which the header/Modified reflects) but not EXIF. Hmm.\n\nWait, but after \"Set Current Time\" save, Modified became 11:21 (details), and header 11:21. That suggests the file was rewritten at 11:21 (modified timestamp), not that capture date was saved. So the header/Modified at 11:21 is just the file modification time from the save. So the header likely shows \"Modified\" date/time. That makes sense! The header displays the photo's date (probably date taken if available else modified), and it changed to 11:21 because the file was modified at 11:21 by the save. Hmm.\n\nSo: capture date edits are not persisted at all. And the details sheet doesn't show capture date. This is a significant metadata-editing bug. But is it the planted \"capture date read from EXIF\" bug? Possibly: the details panel should display capture date read from EXIF, but since EXIF capture date is never saved, it can't.\n\nWait, but maybe the capture date IS saved to the JPEG EXIF but the app reads it wrong. We can't inspect the file. But repeated reopen shows empty, and there's no other display. From the user's perspective, editing capture date does nothing. That's a bug.\n\nBut hold on — maybe I'm misinterpreting the editor UI: perhaps the Captured field is not meant to be prefilled; maybe it's a \"set new capture date\" action, and the actual EXIF value is shown elsewhere. But the field label \"Captured · yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm\" with hint suggests editing. If prefilled, it would show the value. It doesn't. So likely bug.\n\nLet me test the \"Set Current Time\" path once more and confirm: click Set Current Time → field shows date → Save → reopen → empty. We already did this and got empty. But maybe the save is silently failing because the value has seconds and parser rejects → nothing saved. Yet the first manual \"2020-01-02 03:04\" also failed. So both fail.\n\nHmm, so maybe the metadata Save never persists the capture date due to a parsing bug. That's a concrete bug: \"Capture date cannot be saved (field reverts to empty after Save)\". Let me report this. It's within \"editing photo metadata\".\n\nBut wait, before reporting, let me consider whether the capture date save requires a specific format that I'm not using. The hint says \"yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm\". I used exactly that. \"Set Current Time\" produces \"yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss\". Both should be fine.\n\nLet me also test whether other fields save: Title saved initially (we saw QATitle). Image Description/User Comment? Let me test quickly to confirm Save works for text fields in this same editor session. If text saves and date doesn't, it's a capture-date-specific bug.\n\nLet me type a Title \"T1\" now, save, reopen and see. Actually, we've seen title save work. But it later disappeared after move. Hmm. To isolate date bug, do in same session: set Title \"T2\" and capture \"2021-05-06 07:08\", Save, reopen: check Title persists, capture empty. That's clean.\n\nLet me do that. Type Title. Tap element 5 (Description tab) first? Actually currently Origin tab. Set capture \"2021-05-06 07:08\" now, then switch Description and set Title T2, then Save.\n\nType capture."}
