m is clear and in scope (metadata editing). Let me file:\n\nscreen: EXIF & Metadata Editor > Origin\nelement: Captured field\nfield: Captured\nsymptom_type: not_persisted\nexpected: After entering a capture date (e.g. 2021-05-06 07:08) and saving, reopening the editor shows that capture date.\nobserved: The Captured field shows only the placeholder \"Captured · yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm\" (empty) after Save and reopen, while the Title entered in the same save persists (T2).\n\nelement_ref: 8 (in latest observe, the Captured field).\nobserved_quote: \"Captured · yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm\" — hmm, that's the placeholder text, which is on screen. It demonstrates empty. The instructions say quote exact text you saw; a report about something missing may leave quote out. Here the quote is the placeholder showing instead of the value. That's fine — the placeholder IS on screen. But could be considered \"never on screen\"? It is.\n\nLet me file."}
