etails panel.\n\nLet me consider: If the details sheet should show capture date, then with capture date Jan 2 2020 stored (header shows it), the details sheet should show \"Captured: January 2, 2020\" or similar. It doesn't. So the details panel is NOT reading the capture date. That matches the change note exactly: capture date should be read from EXIF into the details panel, but it's missing. And the header is a separate display (maybe the top bar date is the capture date, which is already read from EXIF — hmm, contradictory).\n\nHmm, wait. If the header shows Jan 2 2020, then the app IS reading capture date from EXIF for the header. So the \"photo details panel\" could be the header. Then no bug there.\n\nMaybe the intended \"photo details panel\" is the metadata editor's Origin tab? No.\n\nLet me look at the details sheet screenshot with the capture date set. Maybe there's a row I overlooked after the title section. Let me screenshot the details sheet now (we're in editor; close). Actually, let me close editor and screenshot the details sheet.\n\nActually, the observe list clearly lacks any capture row. There are 31 elements: title T2, Image Properties (Resolution), File Information (name, Added, Modified, Type, Size, URL, Path). No capture.\n\nHmm, let me look at the header again: \"January 2, 2020 · 3:04 AM\". That's clearly a capture date. The details sheet shows Added/Modified 2026. So the header reads EXIF capture date. So \"photo details panel\" might be the header. Works.\n\nCould the intended bug be the header showing the wrong thing for photos WITHOUT EXIF? It falls back to... For huge.jpg, header shows \"November 14 · 11:19 AM\", which matches Added/Modified. That's reasonable fallback.\n\nHmm. Let me test the header after \"Strip All EXIF\" — if it falls back correctly.\n\nI'm spending a lot. Let me consider that maybe there are no bugs in the three changed items, and the planted bugs are elsewhere in the areas. The task says \"sweep these areas\" not 