rename with a name containing a dot, e.g., \"my.photo\". The field + fixed \".jpg\" → \"my.photo.jpg\". Fine.\n\nWhat about case: rename to \"BIG\" — should work.\n\nWhat about renaming to an existing name in the same folder? Currently Beta has big.jpg and hughugeQ.jpg. If I rename big.jpg to \"hughugeQ\", collision. Let me test and observe. If the app throws an error or overwrites, that's a bug. Let me do it carefully with hughugeQ copy in Zulu? Actually Beta has big.jpg and hughugeQ.jpg. Rename big.jpg → hughugeQ → collision. If it overwrites, data loss (the hughugeQ copy lost). It's a copy, acceptable. But if the app handles it (error), good.\n\nLet me test. We're in the Zulu photo details. Let me go back to big.jpg (element 7 in filmstrip?) Actually easier: navigate to Beta album and open big.jpg, rename to hughugeQ.\n\nActually, let me first test the \"Revert\" and \"Strip All EXIF\" on this Zulu copy (safe, it's a copy). Then I can delete the copies.\n\nTest Revert: In details, Edit metadata & EXIF, change Title to \"ZZZ\", tap Revert → should revert to prior (empty). Let me test.\n\nLet me tap Edit metadata & EXIF (26)."}
