{"type": "thinking", "text": "Title empty. So big.jpg's metadata truly gone. This is a metadata persistence issue. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the app writes metadata to a sidecar/cache that is lost when the file is moved. Big.jpg was moved from Alpha to Beta at 11:27, and the Title T2 was set AFTER the move? Let me re-trace:\n- Moved big.jpg to Beta at ~11:27 (sna \"Moved item to Beta\").\n- Then set Title T2 (at ~11:31?) and capture 2020 (11:32?).\n- Header showed Jan 2 2020.\n- Then title/capture gone, Modified 11:32.\n\nHmm, the Modified 11:32 might be when I saved the capture 2020. So the save did write. Then later, the metadata got lost.\n\nCould the \"Revert\" on the Zulu copy have affected big.jpg? Or the \"Cancel\" after Revert? \n\nWait, maybe the actual cause: I opened the Zulu copy from Media, then its metadata editor, typed ZZZ, tapped Revert, then \"Strip All EXIF\" → Cancel. Then canceled. Hmm.\n\nActually, hold on: maybe the media grid's first item (big.jpg) and the filmstrip order changed, and the photo I opened was not the big.jpg I thought. But desc says big.jpg and path Beta/big.jpg.\n\nI think there's an app-level bug where editing metadata for one photo clobbers another (maybe the app reuses a single temp file or caches EXIF in a shared location). That would be severe. But hard to pin.\n\nLet me try a clean, controlled test to see if metadata persists for a photo that is NOT moved/renamed afterward:\n- Take the Zulu copy (hughugeQ in Zulu). Set Title \"PERSIST\" via editor, Save. Confirm details shows Title PERSIST. Then leave the app/photo, do something else (e.g., view another photo, go to Albums, come back), reopen the same photo and check Title. If it persists, then the earlier loss was due to later operations (move/rename).\n- Then maybe move it to another album and check if Title persists. That would test metadata loss on move.\n\nLet me do this on the Zulu copy. First cancel this editor (13) and close details, open the Zulu copy.\n\nActually, I'm burning steps. Let me be strategic. The likely intended bugs may be simpler. Let me look at the size formatting once more but check the *album card* or *list view* sizes, and also the \"Resolution\" maybe.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider the possibility that the intended bug is in the move dialog ordering and I mis-tested. Let me re-test the Move dialog ordering with a clearer set of album names, e.g., create albums \"aaa\" and \"zzz\" and \"mmm\" so alphabetical vs insertion differs. We have Alpha, Beta, IrisSeed, Zulu. The move dialog for big.jpg (in Beta) should list Alpha, IrisSeed, Zulu. Insertion order: IrisSeed (original), Zulu (created), Alpha (created). Alphabetical: Alpha, IrisSeed, Zulu. If we see Alpha first, it's alphabetical. Let me test now: big.jpg is in Beta. Open More → Move to album and observe order. That's a clean test because Alpha (insertion last) should appear first if alphabetical.\n\nEarlier we tested big.jpg in Alpha → dialog listed Beta, IrisSeed, Zulu (alphabetical). Insertion order was IrisSeed, Zulu, Beta. So Beta first proved alphabetical. Good, already confirmed. So ordering works.\n\nSo move dialog ordering = correct.\n\nHmm, maybe the bug is the count \"1 items\" in the move dialog (grammar). Or the \"New album\" card positioned first (not alphabetical) — the requirement says albums in the dialog are listed alphabetically; \"New album\" is not an album. Fine.\n\nLet me look at the byte counts again — maybe there is a bug when the size is in KB range. We don't have such files. The precondition values are MB. So can't test KB.\n\nHmm, maybe the app's size formatting uses 1024 divisors but the *decimal separator* or *unit* is wrong for exactly 1,500,000: maybe it should be \"1.4 MB\" and we see \"1.4 MB\". Fine.\n\nOK, let me now seriously consider that the planted bugs could be:\n1. The capture date is read from EXIF (header works) BUT the details sheet doesn't show it → intended bug.\n2. The \"1 items\" pluralization → maybe.\n3. The metadata not persisting after some operations → maybe.\n\nLet me test the metadata persistence more cleanly to find a reproducible bug:\n\nTest: On the Zulu copy (hughugeQ in Zulu), set Title \"PERSIST\" and save. Then navigate away (to Albums and back) and reopen → does Title persist? If yes, metadata persists normally. Then move the photo to another album (e.g., Beta) and reopen → does Title persist? If lost on move, that's a solid bug: moving loses metadata.\n\nThis tests the \"editing metadata, renaming and moving photos\" area comprehensively. Let me do it.\n\nSteps:\n1. Cancel current editor (big.jpg).\n2. Close details.\n3. Back to Media.\n4. Open Zulu copy (element 6 top-right).\n5. Details → Edit metadata → Description → Title \"PERSIST\" → Save.\n6. Verify details shows Title PERSIST; close details; header title PERSIST.\n7. Navigate: back to Media, open another photo, come back, open Zulu copy → check Title persists.\n8. Move Zulu copy to Beta (More → Move to album → Beta). Then reopen from Beta → check Title.\n9. Restore/cleanup.\n\nLet me do it.\n\nCancel editor."}
